# =====================================================================
# rb4011_dns_resolver_delta — resolver chain per VLAN (DHCP + /ip dns)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Transient delta: sets the DHCP dns-server chain per VLAN — VPS PRIMARY ->
# oldsrv SECONDARY -> Pi TERTIARY, HOME-FIRST (Pi -> VPS -> oldsrv) on every VLAN
# whose `network_vlans` row carries `lan_first_dns: true`.
#
# RouterOS /ip dhcp-server network takes AT MOST 3 dns-server values (a 4th is
# silently dropped), so the router's own /ip dns is not in the DHCP list — it is
# the implicit final fallback for clients that reach none of the three.
#
# The ORDER is not cosmetic: the instances answer the home-hosted app names with
# DIFFERENT addresses, so whichever a VLAN queries first decides whether that VLAN
# sees the home edge or the VPS edge (docs/network-dns.md §Per-Instance Split-Horizon).
# A home-first chain is WAN/VPS-outage resilience for that VLAN.
#
# Final state is ALSO folded into rb4011_converge.rsc.j2 (whose idempotency is
# partial by design — an /add duplicate aborts before the DNS section) and into
# roles/router/tasks/main.yml — all three read the same `lan_first_dns` SSOT.
# Render: playbooks/render-converge.yml; apply: scripts/routeros-apply-delta.sh.
# =====================================================================
# DHCP — per-VLAN resolver chain (3 max), rendered from the `network_vlans` SSOT
{% for v in network_vlans %}
/ip dhcp-server network set [find where address={{ v.subnet }}] dns-server={{ ([dns_tertiary_ip, dns_primary_ip, dns_secondary_ip] if (v.lan_first_dns | default(false)) else [dns_primary_ip, dns_secondary_ip, dns_tertiary_ip]) | join(',') }}
{% endfor %}
# Router resolver upstream — VPS,oldsrv,Pi + Cloudflare last (final unfiltered resort)
/ip dns set allow-remote-requests=yes servers={{ dns_primary_ip }},{{ dns_secondary_ip }},{{ dns_tertiary_ip }},1.1.1.1,1.0.0.1
# =====================================================================